{%- set headIntro -%}<p class="page-intro">Harvington's parish church is <strong>St James the Great</strong> in Church Street, and Norton's is <strong>St Egwin's</strong> on Evesham Road. They share a Sunday rota with the churches at Church Lench, Rous Lench and Abbots Morton, all part of the ARCH Benefice, so the place and time of each service move from week to week.</p>
    <p>St Peter's at Abbots Morton, a Grade I listed church on the site of a Saxon one, has a 14th-century tower and a 15th-century roof whose beams are often little more than roughly shaped branches. The moated site of the abbots of Evesham's country retreat lies close by.</p>
    <p class="small"><a href="https://www.archbenefice.org.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ARCH Benefice website &rarr;</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.archbenefice.org.uk/information/arch-messenger" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ARCH Messenger (monthly magazine) &rarr;</a></p>{%- endset -%}
{%- set servicesNote -%}<p>Check the date before you set off, as each Sunday's services are at different churches. {{ services.midweek }} <span class="small muted">Taken from the {{ services.source }}.</span></p>{%- endset -%}
{%- set readingsNote -%}<p class="small muted">Tap a reading to open it in the NRSV (Anglicised) on Bible Gateway.</p>{%- endset -%}
{%- set noServices -%}<p>The next few weeks' services aren't listed here yet. The ARCH Messenger will have them.</p>{%- endset -%}
